et me test SSH connectivity/auth first (non-interactively) so it doesn't hang on a password prompt, then run the copy if key-auth works.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$h = \\\"admin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net\\\"\\n# is ssh present?\\n$ssh = Get-Command s\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;31m      \u2717 Exit code 255 ssh: C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\OpenSSH\\ssh.exe \u001b[31;1mWarning: Permanently added 'siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 The SIFT box is **reachable** (tailnet works \u2014 host key cached), but SSH **rejected non-interactive auth**: `Permission denied (publickey,passw\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 I'll generate the keypair locally (I can do that non-interactively); installing the public key on the SIFT box needs the password once, so that\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$kd = \\\"$env:USERPROFILE\\\\.ssh\\\"\\nif(-not (Test-Path $kd)){ New-Item -ItemType Directory -\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;32m      \u2713 ok\u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m  (205 chars)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 Key's ready (existing keypair reused). **One interactive step is yours** \u2014 install the public key on the SIFT box (enter `admin2`'s password on\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mRead\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"file_path\": \"C:\\\\xp\\\\ssh.txt\"}\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;32m      \u2713 ok\u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m  (10 chars)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 Got it \u2014 using the password from that file to install the key (one-time), then everything else runs key-based. Setting it up now:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$h = \\\"admin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net\\\"\\n$pw = (Get-Content C:\\\\xp\\\\ssh.txt -Raw\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;32m      \u2713 ok\u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m  (20 chars)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 Key installed (`KEY_INSTALLED`). Now verifying key auth works and running the transfer + verification non-interactively:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$h = \\\"admin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net\\\"\\n\\\"=== 1) key-auth test ===\\\"\\nssh -o Ba\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;31m      \u2717 Exit code 255 === 1) key-auth test === \u001b[31;1madmin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net: Permission denied (publickey,pa\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 Key auth still rejected even though the install ran via password \u2014 usually a permissions/StrictModes issue on the remote home or `authorized_ke\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$h = \\\"admin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net\\\"\\n$pw = (Get-Content C:\\\\xp\\\\ssh.txt -Raw\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;32m      \u2713 ok\u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m  (495 chars)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 Permissions and the key are correct on the remote \u2014 so the most likely cause is the **pre-existing private key has a passphrase** (BatchMode ca\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$h = \\\"admin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net\\\"\\n$nk = \\\"$env:USERPROFILE\\\\.ssh\\\\id_agen\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;31m      \u2717 Exit code 255 new pubkey: ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIBbmjK8S6b+lHRtN5K59YJM7ZjVJYu9uvCCch5yWzJtO agentro-veri\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 Not a passphrase issue (fresh passphraseless key, explicit `-i`, still rejected). Key + perms are correct, so the server is refusing pubkey for\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$h = \\\"admin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net\\\"\\n$pw = (Get-Content C:\\\\xp\\\\ssh.txt -Raw\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;32m      \u2713 ok\u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m  (1298 chars)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 The auth log reveals the key **does** work now: `Accepted publickey for admin2 from 100.70.202.50`. Pubkey auth is functioning. Let me run a cl\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$h = \\\"admin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net\\\"\\n$k1 = \\\"$env:USERPROFILE\\\\.ssh\\\\id_ed25\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;31m      \u2717 Exit code 255 --- clean key-auth test (BatchMode, explicit keys) --- \u001b[31;1madmin2@siftworkstation.taile7c9ca.ts.net: P\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 The real bug: my `-N '\"\"'` (single-quoted) gave the key a **literal `\"\"` passphrase** instead of none \u2014 so BatchMode can't use it; it only work\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1;36m  \u25b8 \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37mPowerShell\u001b[0m  \u001b[0;37m{\"command\": \"$nk = \\\"$env:USERPROFILE\\\\.ssh\\\\id_agentro\\\"\\nRemove-Item \\\"$nk\\\",\\\"$nk.pub\\\" -ErrorAction\u2026\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;32m      \u2713 ok\u001b[0m\u001b[0;90m  (129 chars)\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0;33m  \u2301 Now it's genuinely passphraseless. Installing it and running the full transfer + verification:\u001b[0m"]
